{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And there shall be no plague among the children of Israel, when the children of Israel come near to the sanctuary.</b> For the Levites will prevent them from entering and coming within their precinct. And you will find in this verse five occurrences of 'Israel,' for Scripture mentions them several times in one place by way of endearment, preeminence, and honor — like a person who mentions his son constantly in every single utterance. And our Rabbis of blessed memory drew a parable for this: to a child who went to school, and his father came to ask about him — 'Did my son eat? Did my son drink? Is my son well? Did my son go to school? Did my son come back from school?' — mentioning him in every single utterance by way of endearment. And so too the matter of the Mishkan (Tabernacle), which is mentioned five times in the Torah, and all by way of endearment and honor. And the reason for five in connection with Israel and with the Mishkan: it corresponds to the five fifths of the Torah, which is the sustenance of the world that was created with the letter ה, as it is said (Genesis 2:4): ״בהבראם״ — 'when they were created' — read as בה׳ בראם, 'with ה He created them.' For it [the Torah] was fit to be given only to Israel, and Israel endure only for the sake of the Torah; and it is known concerning the Mishkan, that it and its vessels are a model of this world, which was created with ה."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:30:49.646287898Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}